==NOTE== : 
Initializing variables is must.This will raise a NameError, as the interpreter cannot find the name in any of the accessible scopes. It is crucial to always initialize a variable by assigning it a value before its first use


# Data Types

Data types are classifications that instruct the interpreter on how to store, interpret, and operate on data.

In Python's object-oriented model, these data types are implemented as classes, and variables are instances (objects) of these classes 

In python Everything is a object.

- Numeric : int,float,complex
- sequence : list,string,tuple
- mapping : dict
- set : set,frozenset
- boolean : bool

###### Numeric

int : arbitary` precision (no max limit) , time on operations increases with increase in precision

float : 64bit (8 byte)
complex : 128bit 

